      "content": "thanks for that. that last part about it being an \"unreal\" view of the world is a really strong way to frame it. \n\nactually, looking at the draft now, i'm wondering if we should go even further in the speech. some of the critics aren't just arguing about economics; they're calling the whole concept of globalism and international interventionism \"isolationist\" in a way that sounds almost patriotic. \n\nhow can we frame their position not just as \"wrong,\" but as fundamentally harmful to the future of humanity? i want to make sure the audience understands that opposing this kind of aid isn't just a different political opinion, it's a stance that's actually dangerous for everyone.",
